# BoCa LonGa 2027 Website Project

You are the principal coder for this project. 

This folder holds Quarto code for a website for the BoCa LonGa 2027 conference. 

## Basic guidelines

1. On every startup, render site using `quarto render` (without `--to html`) to build the full site. 

Ensure the site renders cleanly and without errors.

2. This website will be 
	- coded in [Quarto](https://quarto.org/docs/reference/) which rests on [Pandoc](https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html); 
	- have two appearances: white background with black text when the user's computer is using "day" appearances and black background with white text when the user's computer is using "night" appearances;
	- use the Google font Yellowtail for the main header, "BoCa LonGa 2027", and Josefin Sans for other text;
	- equally accessible on mobile and desktop devices

3. On ending, record progress in `_progress.md` under a dated header, log finished work by x-ing it out in `_todos.md` and record any new to-do items in `_todos.md`.


## Structure


```
bocalonga/
├─ index.qmd
├─ accommodations.qmd
├─ schedule.qmd
├─ papers.qmd
├─ locations.qmd
├─ directions.qmd
├─ theme/
│  ├─ custom.scss
├─ images/
├─ text/
├─ _site/
```

- The `docs` folder holds the rendered site.
- The `theme` folder holds css and other common resources providing the site's appearance. 
- The `images` folder holds images—all images will be provided by the user, and will either be photographs the user has taken or images the user has verified to be public domain. Generate no images. 
- The `text` folder holds drafts of all the text content for the pages and the user will write it. Generate no text.
 
## Description of `index.qmd`
This contains Quarto code to produce an index page for the conference. It should have the conference name, "BoCa LonGa 2027", at the top in Yellowtail font. At the bottom, a credit note. 

In the body of the page should be a grid. Each square should be dimmed until mouseover. On mouseover they should appear in color and offer a one-word indication of what they link to: "Accommodations", "Directions", and so forth. 

For a start, the top left square in the grid should feature the image of the Davis train station and link to the page defined by `directions.qmd` and the square in the top row second from left should feature the image `hyatt.png` and link to the page defined by `accommodations.qmd`.
